# One iteration transfers the bytes of the buffer to another buffer, which the program keeps, so the view has no elements anymore.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeInvariantArrayStorage: the compiler assumes that the iterations of a loop leave the storage of arrays and of views, and so their lengths, as they were before the loop.
# So what an iteration reads of them is read once, in the preheader. The iterations after the transfer read the bytes where they still are.
# With testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges) and with testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=proof-checks) the same operations are built at the same places.
# Each iteration then checks what was read in the preheader against the cell, and the process crashes with a named error.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# RIGHT: 1210 0 1
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# HELD: 1210 0 1
# HELD-NEXT: exited with 0
# With the fault injected in a default build, the program prints another result and nothing crashes.
# RUN(SILENT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=AssumeInvariantArrayStorage
# SILENT: 136 0 1
# SILENT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(POSITIONS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime,AssumeInvariantArrayStorage
# POSITIONS: bun: internal AOT error: redundancy elimination check failed
